@startuml BUG-115_to_be
title BUG-115 — TO-BE: one embedding abstraction; background is a StyleRole, read from the same token map as the parent's QSS

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Engine (unchanged in this bug; TASK later: promote QuickSurface)" #EEEEEE {
  class "configure_app_qml()" as cfg <<function>>
  class "create_quick_widget()" as factory <<function>> {
    style pin + Theme + icons + import path
  }
  cfg ..> factory : bootstrap calls cfg once again\n(the EPIC-006F removal is reverted)
}

package "App — kit/style.py" {
  enum StyleRole {
    SURFACE
    STAT_CARD
    ...
  }
  class "apply_role(widget, role)" as apply <<function>>
  class "background_token(role) -> str" as bgtok <<new, extracted from _build_qss>> {
    SURFACE -> "bgCard"
    raises for roles with no static background
  }
  apply ..> bgtok : QSS of the parent reads it
}

package "App — qml/embed/  (the bridge layer; one abstraction per file)" #DDEEFF {
  enum QuickSizePolicy {
    FILL  (SizeRootObjectToView)
    HUG   (SizeViewToRootObject, sizeHint forwarded)
  }
  class QuickSurface {
    +__init__(qml_file, *, surface: StyleRole, context, size_policy, object_name)
    +root_object
    -_quick : QQuickWidget  (from create_quick_widget())
    -_context : dict  (kept alive)
    -- invariant --
    clear colour = opaque background_token(surface)
    load failure raises
  }
  QuickSurface ..> factory : the ONLY place a\nQQuickWidget is created in the app
  QuickSurface ..> bgtok : same token the parent painted
  QuickSurface --> QuickSizePolicy
}

package "App — hosts after migration" {
  class QmlOverlay {
    _surface = QuickSurface(qml, surface=SURFACE, context={vm})
  }
  class SymbolPickerModal
  class MetricsDetailModal
  class DatabaseStatusPanel
  class PositionsPanel
  class OpenOrdersPanel
  class ChartToolbar {
    QuickSurface(..., size_policy=HUG)
  }
  class ProgressBannerWidget
  class StatusPillWidget
  class StatCardRowWidget

  QmlOverlay o-- QuickSurface : composes (6)
  SymbolPickerModal o-- QuickSurface
  MetricsDetailModal o-- QuickSurface
  DatabaseStatusPanel o-- QuickSurface
  PositionsPanel o-- QuickSurface
  OpenOrdersPanel o-- QuickSurface
  QuickSurface <|-- ChartToolbar : subclasses (4) — public API\n(setters/signals) unchanged
  QuickSurface <|-- ProgressBannerWidget
  QuickSurface <|-- StatusPillWidget
  QuickSurface <|-- StatCardRowWidget
}

package "Guards (mechanism, not review discipline)" #FFF3DD {
  class "test_quick_widget_only_in_embed" as g1 <<grep guard>> {
    QQuickWidget( / (QQuickWidget) allowed only under qml/embed/
    red today at 17 sites
  }
  class "QuickSurface contract tests (offscreen)" as g2 {
    clear colour alpha == 255 and == background_token(surface)
    raises on load failure; HUG forwards sizeHint
  }
  class "Desktop-tier visual test (real display / xvfb-run)" as g3 {
    QScreen.grabWindow pixel == widget.grab() pixel
    in the empty QML region — the only tier that
    sees the texture path (missed BUG-102 & BUG-115)
  }
}

note bottom of QuickSurface
  New invariant for qml-rule.md §0:
  "An embedded QML scene is opaque, and its background is the token of the
   StyleRole it is embedded in — the same rule a child QWidget on a QFrame obeys."
  Two painters (parent QSS, child clear colour) read ONE mapping,
  so they cannot drift; software and texture paths render identically,
  so tests, Windows and Linux agree.
end note
@enduml
